\subsection{Definitions and mathematical statement}
\paragraph{Statement recorded in the supplied source.}
For the symmetric four-state broadcast channel $P(j|i)=\lambda $ $1_{i=j}+(1-\lambda )/4$ with $0<\lambda <1$, is reconstruction on every d-ary tree, integer $d\geq 2$, and on the observed Poisson(d) offspring tree for every real $d>0$ possible exactly when d $\lambda ^2>1$, with nonreconstruction at equality?

